The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says the 412 merged reports are one bug. They are three.
Each has its own cause and needs its own fix and its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. A parser fix alone leaves 38 of the 412 reports open.
</Callout>

## What the 412 reports hold

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

1. **`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Tenants that write the day first
   get day and month flipped. This is the bug the #4471 page describes.
2. **`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** People at day-first tenants
   (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) type what the hint tells them. The form reads it
   their way. Only `form` reports. Intake tagged 15 of these 33 as `parser`, so a parser fix
   will not help them. The fix is the hint on booking-v3.
3. **`one-day`: dates move by exactly one day.** This is not a month and day flip. The desk
   notes already read 5 reports this way, but the table on the #4471 page counts them under
   `parser`. Two of them point at time zones. The cause is not confirmed.

## How the reports were placed

- The ticket export has repeated rows. One id is one report: 427 rows, 412 reports.
- Cause comes from the **tenant** (its locale and booking form), not from intake's browser
  guess. The rule is in `causeOf` in `causes.ts`.
- One-day moves come from `desk-notes.json`.

## Tickets

One GitHub issue per problem, each with its report count:
[issue 1](https://github.com/pkulikow/what-it-shows-4471/issues/1) (parser),
[issue 2](https://github.com/pkulikow/what-it-shows-4471/issues/2) (hint),
[issue 3](https://github.com/pkulikow/what-it-shows-4471/issues/3) (one-day).

## Lessons

- Merging on a subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) joined
  reports that only look alike. Read the body and the tenant before you merge.
- A count in the title of a ticket hides how many bugs sit under it.

